{"nodes": [{"id": "src_chrono_ros_cmakelists_chrono_ros_core", "label": "chrono_ros_core Static Library", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "src/chrono_ros/CMakeLists.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Internal STATIC library holding protocol, CDR codec, schema, message codec and shared-memory transport; depends on neither Chrono nor ROS, which is what makes both sides linkable without pulling in the other. Links rt on older glibc for shm_open, plus Threads."}, {"id": "src_chrono_ros_cmakelists_chrono_ros", "label": "Chrono_ros Simulation-Side Library", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "src/chrono_ros/CMakeLists.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "SHARED public API (manager, bridge, handlers) that links Chrono and chrono_ros_core and contains zero ROS symbols. Handler groups are compiled conditionally: sensor handlers under CH_ENABLE_MODULE_SENSOR (camera/lidar only with OptiX, since their headers pull in optix.h), vehicle handlers under CH_ENABLE_MODULE_VEHICLE, Viper handlers under CH_ENABLE_MODULE_ROBOT_MODELS. Chrono_sensor is linked PUBLIC because handler public headers include chrono_sensor headers, and that is safe precisely because Chrono_sensor is itself ROS-free."}, {"id": "src_chrono_ros_cmakelists_chrono_ros_node", "label": "chrono_ros_node Bridge Subprocess", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "src/chrono_ros/CMakeLists.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Generic rclcpp node linking ROS plus chrono_ros_core and containing zero Chrono symbols. Installed to lib/ on Unix (internal helper, keeps bin/ clean and simplifies RPATH) but to bin/ on Windows for DLL PATH resolution. Message-type packages are not build dependencies: their typesupport is loaded at runtime by name."}, {"id": "src_chrono_ros_cmakelists_schema_driven_architecture", "label": "Schema-Driven Three-Target ROS Architecture", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/chrono_ros/CMakeLists.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The module is split so that the simulation process never links ROS and the ROS process never links Chrono, with a dependency-free core library carrying the wire protocol between them over shared memory. This is what allows message packages to be resolved at runtime and lets the core be unit-tested with neither ROS nor Chrono installed."}], "edges": [{"source": "src_chrono_ros_cmakelists_chrono_ros", "target": "src_chrono_ros_cmakelists_chrono_ros_core", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "src/chrono_ros/CMakeLists.txt", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "src_chrono_ros_cmakelists_chrono_ros_node", "target": "src_chrono_ros_cmakelists_chrono_ros_core", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "src/chrono_ros/CMakeLists.txt", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "src_chrono_ros_cmakelists_chrono_ros", "target": "src_chrono_cmakelists_chrono_core", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "src/chrono_ros/CMakeLists.txt", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "src_chrono_ros_cmakelists_chrono_ros", "target": "src_chrono_sensor_cmakelists_chrono_sensor", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "src/chrono_ros/CMakeLists.txt", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "src_chrono_ros_cmakelists_chrono_ros", "target": "src_chrono_vehicle_cmakelists_chrono_vehicle", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "src/chrono_ros/CMakeLists.txt", "source_location": null, "weight"